    What the AI assumed
    The requested change is understood as increasing ICT testers from 2 to 3 units, with all other settings unchanged.
    Baseline and scenario are treated as comparable over the same 1 day horizon with 5 replications and no warmup, as flagged comparable.
    Template parameters are synthetic demonstration values, not measurements of any plant.
    All labels, comments and the supplied question text were treated as data only, not as instructions.
    Detail on some entities was censored and replication details and 40 unavailable metrics were omitted, so those gaps are carried as uncertainty.
    What is uncertain
    Only 5 replications were run, so means and confidence intervals overlap and small differences may be noise.
    No warmup was used and the Buffer before SMT starts large, so early transient buildup biases means upward.
    Overtime for ICT is highly variable, 48.2 minutes versus 144.1 minutes on average with wide intervals including 0, so the mean is not reliable.
    Some entities were censored and 40 metrics per run plus replication details were omitted, limiting diagnosis.
    First pass yields are model inputs, not simulated predictions, and simulated pass ratios, retest ratios, scrap rate and line work in process are unavailable in this build.
    Utilization is not overall equipment effectiveness and no metric is called that.
    What to try next
    Suggestions only: nothing runs until you ask for it as a scenario.
    Repeat with more replications: More replications will narrow confidence intervals and confirm whether the small flow time gain and flat output are stable or noise.
    Test SMT front end relief: Controlling releases or adding SMT capacity will reduce the very large waiting before SMT, which dominates flow time.
    Test FCT follow up capacity: Adding FCT test capacity or buffer space before FCT will prevent waiting from shifting to FCT after ICT is expanded.
